  "description": "A lean, dependency-light .NET 8 SDK for Solana. JSON-RPC reads, send/simulate, and multiplexed WebSocket streaming; Ed25519 keys and signing; SPL Token, PDA, and ATA helpers; and spec-accurate legacy and v0 (versioned) transaction building, signing, and decoding — every wire format checked byte-for-byte against the Rust solana-sdk. Ships as one package bundling the Core, Wallet, Rpc, and Programs assemblies.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "SolSharp",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-01T22:38:51.953Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "mVozgMp0Eq/GSicV5u2Tw7WfkICxJEbiNEyLKd/118m1NLoNtAS7xIKVn2KfdoNAbeF9zEtk5+PLfpdeINljNw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 218835,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/jecacs/SolSharp",
  "published": "2026-07-01T22:34:44.31Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.5.0 adds durable-nonce support (NonceAccount decoding, GetNonceAccountAsync, TransactionBuilder.SetDurableNonce), BIP-39/SLIP-0010 mnemonic wallet import (Keypair.FromMnemonic / FromMnemonicAtPath), and new instructions: System AllocateWithSeed/AssignWithSeed/TransferWithSeed, SPL Token SetAuthority + ApproveChecked/MintToChecked/BurnChecked, Compute Budget RequestHeapFrame/SetLoadedAccountsDataSizeLimit, and ATA CreateIdempotent. It also hardens SolanaWsClient (a rejected subscribe faults instead of hanging; an undecodable notification faults only its own subscription; DisposeAsync completes channels) and wire parsing (FormatException on truncated data, versioned-message version check, PDA/lookup-table limits); memo signers are now read-only, matching the Rust spl-memo builder. Follows semantic versioning; while on 0.x, minor releases may carry breaking changes. Changelog: https://github.com/jecacs/SolSharp/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
